<title>USA: Wage talks at BHP Copper's US plants start Tuesday.</title>
<headline>Wage talks at BHP Copper's US plants start Tuesday.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Union leaders at BHP Copper's U.S. operations in San Manuel and Pinto Valley in Arizona will ask for a large pay hike when wage talks on behalf of 4,000 employees start Tuesday, a union official said.</p>
<p>&quot;We are asking for a significant increase,&quot; lead negotiator Robert Guadiana of the United Steelworkers of America said, declining to disclose any further details.</p>
<p>Workers at the two plants signed a 15-year framework deal June 1991 with provision for review every five years.</p>
<p>The review period began February 19 this year, but until now only the non-economic aspects were being discussed.</p>
<p>&quot;If we don't reach agreement by July 1, we then go to interest arbitration,&quot; Guadiana said.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1646))</p>
